{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Access approvals (spec §3.13). A requesting device encrypts the subject (metadata only, never a value) under VK[key_epoch] and signs the request; an approving device of the same account signs a decision bound to the request digest. key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm=VK[e], salt=b64decode(request_id), info=utf8(\"akv1/approval-request\"), L=32) with VK[e] from seal-key.json seal_keys[].vk; aad = cjson({\"ctx\":\"akv1/approval-request\",\"vault_id\",\"request_id\",\"key_epoch\",\"requester\",\"ts\",\"expires_at\"}); ct = XChaCha20-Poly1305(key, n, cjson(subject), aad); sig = Ed25519 under context \"akv1/approval-request\" over the wire minus sig. digest = b64(SHA-256(cjson(request wire, sig included))). decision sig = Ed25519 under \"akv1/approval-decision\" over the decision minus sig. cases: sealApprovalRequest with the given nonce wire.n and request_id MUST reproduce wire byte for byte (Ed25519 is deterministic), openApprovalRequest MUST yield subject, and approvalRequestDigest MUST equal digest. openApprovalRequest order: parse (v or alg unknown: unsupported_version; exact keys, IDs, n 24 B, ct 16..16400 B, sig 64 B, expires_at > ts: bad_request); vault_id other than expected (bad_request); signature under the requester sign_pub (invalid_signature); AEAD (decrypt_failed); subject not canonical, unknown or missing keys, fingerprint not sha256:<64 hex>, max_ttl_s outside 60..2592000, empty optional text (bad_request). decisions: signApprovalDecision by approver alice-laptop at ts MUST reproduce decision byte for byte and verifyApprovalDecision(decision, cases[0].wire, {approver sign_pub, max_ttl_s 86400}) MUST accept it. verifyApprovalDecision order: parse (unsupported_version / bad_request; ttl_s present exactly for allow_ttl, 60..2592000); request_id, vault_id, requester or request_digest other than the request (bad_request); ts outside [request.ts, request.expires_at) (bad_request); ttl_s above max_ttl_s (bad_request); signature (invalid_signature). invalid: openApprovalRequest MUST fail with expect_error. decision_invalid: verifyApprovalDecision MUST fail with expect_error.",
